# Multi-Feature Architecture

The Finance Simulator is one SPA hosting multiple **features** (not separate apps).
Users switch features with a tab bar; there is no per-feature runtime isolation.
Background jobs keep running across tab switches.

## Naming

- **App**: "Finance Simulator"; app-wide prefix is **`fs`**.
- **Feature ids** (kebab-case): `sor-plan` → "SOR Plan"; `sor-lab` → "SOR Lab".
- Folders: `src/features/<feature-id>/` for feature-owned logic, UI, and partials.
- DOM: feature roots `id="feature-<feature-id>"`; new element ids prefixed
  `<feature-id>-...`. Existing SOR Plan ids are renamed only opportunistically.

## Shared vs feature code

| Lives in | Examples |
|---|---|
| Shared (`src/core`, `src/ui`, `src/state`, `src/workers`, `src/partials/shared/`) | Scenario model + defaults/presets, RNG, sensitivity summarizer (`sensitivity.js`), workers, chart theme/setup, dialogs, header, session chrome, feature registry, session/job abstractions |
| Feature (`src/features/<id>/`) | Feature partials, input wiring, results/report UI, feature charts, run orchestration, Lab variable registry |

Truly shared code stays shared. Risk-preset *data* (`src/state/presets/`) stays
shared with the scenario model; only the Easy Mode UI lives under the feature.
Feature-specific code must not reach into another feature's DOM or module state —
consume scenarios only through `scenario.js` / session-store interfaces.

SOR Lab keeps sweep *results* in memory (config + Plan dependency snapshots are
what save/share). Visualizations read stored curves through pure selectors — do
not bake tornado-only shapes into the persisted result model.

## Storage namespaces

- localStorage:
  - `fs:app:<key>` — genuinely cross-feature prefs only (theme, active tab).
  - `fs:<feature-id>:<key>` — feature state (autosave, report band, accordions,
    chart view prefs). **When in doubt, use the feature namespace.**
- IndexedDB: single `fs-sessions` database, `sessions` store, records keyed by
  `[feature, name]` (Phase 2+).
- Export envelope: `type: "fs-scenario"` plus `feature` and per-feature
  `stateVersion`; dependency snapshots carry their own `feature` +
  `stateVersion` + `state`. Legacy `sor-scenario` *file* import remains the
  only backward-compat path (its file field is still `schemaVersion`).
- **Clean break**: ignore legacy `sor:*` localStorage keys and the old
  `sor-sessions` IndexedDB database. Legacy share-link URL params are ignored
  (open fresh, no decode, no error). Do not dual-read envelope
  `schemaVersion` on `fs-scenario` payloads.

### State versioning & migrations

- Every session record, export/share envelope, and dependency snapshot writes
  **`stateVersion`** for that feature (Plan uses `SCHEMA_VERSION`; Lab uses
  `LAB_STATE_VERSION`).
- All migrate implementations and the dispatch registry live in
  [`src/state/migrations.js`](../../src/state/migrations.js)
  (`migrateScenario`, `migrateLabState`, `registerFeatureMigrator`,
  `migrateFeatureState`). Persistence / sessions call the registry only —
  no per-feature `if` branches.
- Session adapters may declare `stateVersion` + `migrate`;
  `registerSessionAdapter` re-registers them into the same registry.
- Share links: full URL must be ≤ **8000** characters; over the limit, show
  “Share link is too large. Use Export instead.” and do not copy. Export is
  unrestricted.

## Feature registry

Register features via `src/state/features.js` (`registerFeature`,
`setActiveFeature`, `setFeatureBadge`, …). Tab bar under the title is rendered
from the registry. Active tab persists in `fs:app:prefs`.

### Placement (`primary` | `more`)

- `registerFeature({ …, placement })` — omit or `'primary'` for top-level tabs;
  `'more'` puts the feature under the More control (button + listbox).
- **Primary today:** `sor-plan`, `accumulation`. **More today:** `sor-lab` (plus
  future features). More is always rendered, even if empty.
- When a More feature is active, the More control’s label becomes that feature’s
  title and the control is `aria-selected`. Escape closes the menu and returns
  focus to the More button.
- Busy/progress badges roll up onto the More control when any More feature has a
  running job; each menu item also shows its own badge.
- Narrow viewports keep equal-width cells for the primary tabs **plus More** —
  not one cell per every registered feature.

## Sessions & jobs (Phase 2+)

- Header session controls bind to the **active feature's** session store.
- Share/export payloads are feature-aware and self-contained: feature id + state +
  snapshot copies of cross-feature dependencies. On open/import, embed
  dependencies as named sessions with collision auto-rename — never overwrite
  the recipient's existing sessions.
- Jobs run through a shared job manager; they survive tab switches; results
  deliver to the owning feature; tabs show busy/progress badges.
- **Do not render Chart.js into a hidden feature root** (`display:none` sizes to
  zero). Defer render until `onActivate`, or call `chart.resize()` on activation.
